  "id": "COMPOUND:746 - DISEASE:829",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between irinotecan and Diabetic Angiopathies through a complex network of molecular interactions involving the ubiquitin conjugating enzyme E2 L3. Irinotecan is implicated in affecting this enzyme, which in turn is associated with conditions such as lactase persistence/nonpersistence and non-severe combined immunodeficiency, all of which are linked to Diabetic Angiopathies. The evidence indicates that the enzyme E2 L3 plays a role in the pathogenesis of Diabetic Angiopathies, possibly through its involvement in cellular processes that are disrupted by irinotecan. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact mechanism by which irinotecan influences the enzyme and subsequently leads to Diabetic Angiopathies remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a pathway where irinotecan may modulate the enzyme E2 L3, contributing to the development of diabetic angiopathies, but further research is needed to confirm this relationship and understand the precise molecular interactions involved.",
